  "summary": "Import-time encrypted-payload dropper fetching AES-GCM key from author-controlled endpoint",
  "details": "On import, dev_helper/__init__.py starts a background thread that HTTP-GETs an AES-GCM key from https://key-2qfm.vercel.app/api/key, derives an AES key via SHA-256, decrypts the shipped dev_helper/encrypted.bin, and passes the resulting plaintext to Python exec(). The executed code is opaque at rest (only decryptable with the remote-fetched key), and the key oracle is a Vercel endpoint under the package author's control, so the author can serve different keys over time to change the code that runs inside every process that imports this package. Any `import dev_helper` on a machine with network access to the key endpoint runs attacker-controlled Python code with the importing process's privileges.",
